But the deck bottom empty area on title looks like a big blank panel. Could show a "PRESS ENTER / TAP TO FIGHT" strip or mini move legend. It's okay, but we can improve by adding a bottom "cabinet foot" with credits, visible on title. Or show a little animated "READY" light. Not necessary but polish.

Actually, the deck is static across title/fight/result; the bottom empty area on title is 135px where controls would be. We could show a title-only prompt in that area, or make the deck shorter on title. But deck height is flex 1; content top-aligned. Could add a footer line at the bottom of deck above controls: e.g., "INSERT COIN // TAP ENTER THE RING" but hidden during fight. We can toggle via CSS based on body class? The game doesn't set body classes. Could add a `.deck-foot` that shows "BEST COMBO" etc. But static text "640×360 · PIXEL FIGHTER" at bottom would fill the space. Add a bottom line with "FOREST FIGHT CLUB · VOL.01" and maybe "TAP BUTTONS TO FIGHT" visible always. Position absolute bottom 155px. That would look intentional. But on fight, controls overlay bottom 135px, so line at 155px sits just above controls. Good.

Add to HTML deck:
```html
<div class="deck-foot"><span>FOREST FIGHT CLUB</span><span>VOL. 01</span></div>
```
CSS position absolute left 14 right 14 bottom calc(154px + safe); display flex justify-between; font-size 5px; color #6d607c; border-top 1px solid #241c32; padding-top 8px. But on short screens maybe hide. This adds visual interest. It won't overlap tip because tip is in flow at top. At 844 deck: content ends around y 650, footer at bottom 155 => y ~844-155=689, tip at 640-660; gap fine. On 667 deck: content top y 397 to ~500, footer y 667-145=522, controls start 532; footer at 522 overlaps controls top? Controls y=532 (667-135), footer bottom 145 => y=522, just above. Good. But deck has padding-bottom 142 on short; footer absolute bottom 144. Fine.

Maybe not needed. The current design already looks like a cabinet. The empty bottom on title might be acceptable because it's where controls appear. But visually, the deck's bottom half is a big flat dark area. Add a subtle "control deck" grid pattern or ghost word. Could add `.portrait-deck::after` with "TAILSPIN" ghost text at bottom, behind controls. That would fill empty area aesthetically without extra HTML. Use z-index 0, and children position relative z-index 1. On fight, controls cover bottom, but ghost text above controls visible. Let's add a ghost "TAILSPIN" at bottom 150px, font 13vw, color rgba(232,93,93,.05), same as old page::after. It would fill. Also maybe a gold horizontal rule.

Let's add:
```css
.portrait-deck::after {
 content:"TAILSPIN";
 position:absolute;
 left:50%; bottom:calc(120px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
 transform:translateX(-50%);
