}
.portrait-deck > * { position:relative; z-index:1; }
```
But bottom 120 would put it behind controls (controls 135 high), so mostly hidden. Use bottom 150px. On 844 deck, ghost baseline at y 844-150=694, text height ~50 => visible 644-694. Tip ends ~660, overlap slight but ghost is faint. Fine. On 667, bottom 142+? short media overrides padding but not ::after. Add short media `bottom: 140px; font-size: 11vw;`. It will sit around 527, just above controls. Could overlap moves. Maybe hide ghost on short screens.

Alternatively put ghost behind deck content but content covers. Fine.

Let's also add z-index fix and ghost. Then test controls visibility.

Also note in debug screenshot the HUD timer "60" at top center, health bars. Nice. But the topbar "FOREST FIGHT CLUB" at y 5? It is visible above frame. Good.

One more issue: the quick pause/mute buttons inside frame overlap the moon; acceptable.

Now fix stacking. Add `.game-frame { z-index: 2; }` within portrait media. Does z-index require position? game-frame is position relative. Good.

