`setMuted` updates `ui.mute` but not `ui.quickMute`, which is only updated in syncScreens. syncScreens is called on state changes. So quickMute label remains "SFX" after click, but the actual mute works. That's a UI bug for the quick control; users can't tell state. Fix: in quickMute handler, call `syncScreens()` after setMuted, or update text directly inside setMuted. Better move quickMute update into setMuted (and possibly ensure it doesn't get stale). Add:

```js
if (ui.quickMute) {
  ui.quickMute.textContent = muted ? 'OFF' : 'SFX';
  ui.quickMute.classList.toggle('is-muted', muted);
  ui.quickMute.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(muted));
}
```

But syncScreens also sets it. Fine. Also set initial aria-pressed on quickMute? Not existing. Add to HTML maybe `aria-pressed="false"`. Good.

Test showed `quick mute` text SFX after tap. Let's fix.

Also note quickMute click calls ensureAudio which may resume context. Fine.

Another issue: `ui.quickPause` text toggles in syncScreens; togglePause calls syncScreens? Let's check togglePause.

